   "items": [
    {
     "field": "description",
     "fieldId": "description",
     "from": null,
     "fromString": "h3. Why\n\nWith holds now placed in the reservation store at add-to-cart (CORE-18632), the stock count in the inventory database is only decremented after payment capture. Losing that commit is the hardest failure of Checkout V2: the order ships, the shelf count stays high, and the next customer buys an item that is not there.\n\nh3. Scope\n\n* New worker {{shop-worker/src/inventory_sync}} (TypeScript, Node 24, Vitest).\n* Trigger: the payments webhook handler (v2, v3 and the expiry path) produces an {{InventorySyncCommand}} on Kafka once the payment is captured or the hold expires.\n* On capture: decrement the stock in Postgres in one transaction keyed by {{order_id}}, then emit {{InventorySynced}} and release the hold in Redis.\n* On expiry or refund before shipping: release the hold only; the stock count is never touched.\n* A nightly reconcile job lists holds older than 24 h with no matching order and releases them.\n* Guest carts that never reach checkout are never synced.\n\nh3. Dependencies\n\n* SHOP-3537 (reservation store) and SHOP-3543 (Kafka topics, Redis streams) must land first.\n* SHOP-3559 defines the InventorySyncCommand and InventorySynced messages.\n\nh3. Source",
     "to": null,
     "toString": "h3. Why\n\nWith holds now placed in the reservation store at add-to-cart (CORE-18632), the stock count in the inventory database is only decremented after payment capture. Losing that commit is the hardest failure of Checkout V2: the order ships, the shelf count stays high, and the next customer buys an item that is not there.\n\nh3. Scope\n\n* New worker {{shop-worker/src/inventory_sync}} (TypeScript, Node 24, Vitest).\n* Trigger: the payments webhook handler (v2, v3 and the expiry path) produces an {{InventorySyncCommand}} on Kafka once the payment is captured or the hold expires.\n* On capture: decrement the stock in Postgres in one transaction keyed by {{order_id}}, then emit {{InventorySynced}} and release the hold in Redis.\n* On expiry or refund before shipping: release the hold only; the stock count is never touched.\n* A nightly reconcile job lists holds older than 24 h with no matching order and releases them.\n* Guest carts that never reach checkout are never synced.\n\nh3. Dependencies\n\n* SHOP-3537 (reservation store) and SHOP-3543 (Kafka topics, Redis streams) must land first.\n* SHOP-3559 defines the InventorySyncCommand and InventorySynced messages.\n\nh3. Source\n\nRequirement CHK2-P04 in Checkout V2 :: Requirements, design in Checkout V2 :: Architecture and Checkout V2 :: Stock Reservations."
    }
   ]
